  "answer_text": "Depending on your context, **\"Chase Capital Services\"** typically refers to one of two things:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Chase Auto Leasing / Vehicle Titles (United States)\nIf you are in the United States and dealing with a car lease, **Chase Capital Services** is often the legal lessor/owner name listed on vehicle titles and registration documents. \n\nJPMorgan Chase provides private-label auto financing and leasing for several major car brands (most notably **Mazda Capital Services**, **Subaru Motors Finance**, and **Jaguar/Land Rover Financial Group**). If you lease a vehicle through one of these programs, the title of the car will legally be registered under Chase Capital Services. \n\n**When this typically comes up:**\n* **Lease Buyouts:** If you decide to buy out your leased car, Chase Capital Services will need to release the lien or send you a \"clean\" title.\n* **Moving Out of State:** If you move to a new state and need to register your leased car, your new state's DMV will require a Power of Attorney (POA) and the physical title or a title release from Chase Capital Services to transfer the registration. \n* **Selling to a Third Party:** If you sell your leased car to a dealer (like CarMax or Carvana) before your lease matures, they will require a 10-day payoff quote from Chase Capital Services.\n\n**What you should do:** \nIf you need a title release, a Power of Attorney, or payoff documents, do not search for a standalone company. Instead, log into your auto finance portal through **Chase Online**, **Mazda Capital Services**, or **Subaru Motors Finance**, or call the customer service number on your monthly billing statement to speak with Chase Auto customer service directly.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Chase Capital Services Private Limited (India)\nIf you are looking for an independent financial firm, **Chase Capital Services Private Limited** is an Indian financial consultancy and advisory firm established in May 1997. \n\n* **Location:** Headquartered in Chandigarh/Mohali (Punjab), India.\n* **Services:** The company is primarily engaged in corporate advisory services, debt syndication, securitization, currency and commodity trading on recognized Indian exchanges, and IT services. \n* **Note:** This company is a private unlisted firm and is completely unrelated to JPMorgan Chase & Co.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Chase Capital Partners (Historical Private Equity)\nHistorically, **Chase Capital Partners** was the private equity and venture capital arm of Chase Manhattan Bank (before it merged into JPMorgan Chase). After the merger, it was renamed J.P. Morgan Partners. In 2006, the division spun off from the bank and is now known as **CCMP Capital**.",
